        "v": 5,
        "title": "CLI plan mode UI update",
        "summary": "Plan mode UI updated. Base2 prompt now mandates <PLAN> tags for specs. Chat layout moved build buttons to message blocks. Scrubber logic switched to <PLAN> tags. Scope: CLI chat components, hooks, base2 prompt.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T05:46:53.638Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the assistant lays out a plan for your request, it now wraps that plan in clear start and end markers, so the plan shows up neatly formatted instead of as plain text scattered among tool messages. The \"build fast\" and \"build max\" buttons that let you choose how thoroughly the assistant works on your project have moved from sitting above the chat input to appearing right inside the individual message where the plan was presented, so you can kick off the next step without scrolling. If you are chatting with the assistant in plan mode today, you will see the plan displayed as a distinct block and the two action buttons attached to that specific message rather than floating at the bottom of the screen.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "86a7043427fe",
        "at": "2026-09-17T22:38:30.934Z"
